---
source: tests/cli_golden.rs
expression: help
---
AURA CLI - Autonomous Universal Reasoning Architecture

Usage: aura [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  desktop  Run the agent in the desktop window (default with no subcommand)
  run      Run the agent in the terminal, or as a server with `--ui none`
  login    Sign in to zOS, or link a Claude / ChatGPT plan
  logout   Sign out of zOS, or unlink a plan
  whoami   Show the zOS sign-in and linked plans
  auth     Manage linked plans
  hello    Print "Hello, World!" and exit (Spec 01)
  migrate  Phase 4a stub: migrate aura state (no-op today)
  plugins  Manage declarative plugins (Phase 4b)
  runs     Inspect, compare and label recorded runs (`AURA_HOME/runs/`)
  dataset  Export recorded runs as training data
  eval     Run coding eval suites and compare harness arms
  gate     Check Gate's verdicts against what happened
  cloud    Run agents on their own boxd cloud machines
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --mode <MODE>
          Session mode for the desktop window or terminal. Overrides the daemon default (`AURA_DEFAULT_MODE`); the kernel denies any tool call the mode does not allow

          Possible values:
          - agent: Full unrestricted operation subject to user permissions
          - plan:  Read + markdown writes + read-only subprocesses
          - ask:   Read-only (the terminal's `read-only` mode)
          - debug: Read + sandboxed probes only

      --approval <APPROVAL>
          What tool calls ask first: `yolo` runs everything with commands confined to writing inside the working folder, `ask` asks for anything not on the allow list, `strict` asks for everything but reads. Overrides `AURA_TUI_APPROVAL`; `-p` defaults to `yolo` in agent mode

          Possible values:
          - yolo:   Run everything; commands can write only inside the working folder
          - ask:    Ask for anything not on the project's allow list
          - strict: Ask for everything except reads, even what the allow list covers

  -p, --print [<PROMPT>]
          Run one prompt without the terminal UI, print the result, and exit. `-p -`, or `-p` with no prompt, reads the prompt from stdin; piped stdin is appended to a prompt given here

      --terminal
          Run the agent in this terminal instead of the desktop window. Without a display (e.g. over SSH) the terminal is used anyway
          
          [aliases: --tui]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Options for -p:
      --output-format <FORMAT>
          What `-p` prints: the final reply (`text`), one result object (`json`), or one event per line ending with the result (`stream-json`)

          Possible values:
          - text:        The final reply as plain text
          - json:        One JSON object describing the run
          - stream-json: Newline-delimited JSON events, ending with the result object

      --resume <SESSION_ID>
          Continue the saved session with this id (the `session_id` of an earlier run)

  -c, --continue
          Continue the most recent `aura -p` session

      --allowed-tools <TOOLS>...
          Only these tools may run (comma-separated); every other tool is denied

      --disallowed-tools <TOOLS>...
          These tools may not run (comma-separated)

      --max-turns <N>
          Stop after this many model calls

      --max-time <DURATION>
          Stop after this long: `90s`, `45m`, `2h`, or a bare number of minutes. Overrides `AURA_TUI_TURN_TIMEOUT`

      --max-cost-usd <USD>
          Stop once model calls cost more than this many US dollars at API list prices. Overrides `AURA_TUI_MAX_TURN_COST_USD`

  -d, --cwd <DIR>
          Work in this directory instead of the current one

      --model <MODEL>
          Model for this run, or `gate` to let Gate pick one from what you are signed in to. Not saved as the `/model` choice

      --provider <PROVIDER>
          Model provider: `anthropic` (default; local, plan and aura-router models) or `mock`

      --verbose
          Log debug detail to stderr
